      "knowledge_point": "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using the Natural Logarithm",
      "problem": "Find the solution to the equation ${e}^{1-2x}=5$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-2x} & =5 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{1-2x}) & =ln⁡(5) \\\\ 1-2x & =ln⁡(5) \\\\ -2x & =ln⁡(5)-1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1-ln⁡(5)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈-0.305\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
