      "math_academy_id": "q-263178",
      "knowledge_point_id": "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required",
      "problem": "If ${e}^{x+2}-7=2,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2}-7 & =2 \\\\ {e}^{x+2} & =2+7 \\\\ {e}^{x+2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2} & =9 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{x+2}) & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x+2 & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x & =ln⁡(9)-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.197\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
